NDVI is a very commonly used spectral vegetation index for vegetation monitoring, for example, monitoring crop growth and yields. As you will notice in the codeblock below, the evalscript has changed substantially: - we are only using Band 4 and Band 8 as an input into our script. - In the evaluatePixel() function, we calculate NDVI and visualise this using the imgVals array.

